# data-models-relationships

## Core Data Models

1. Case Management Model
- Hierarchical case structure with client, treatment plans, and interventions
- Links to resource recommendations through multi-faceted matching system
- Stores case outcomes and intervention effectiveness metrics
- Path: lib/engine.ts
Importance Score: 90/100

2. Knowledge Base Model  
- Treatment provider data with regional proximity scoring
- Clinical protocols organized by intervention type
- Service capability flags and specialization markers
- Path: lib/knowledge-base.ts
Importance Score: 85/100

3. Research Integration Model
- Evidence-based practice categorization system
- Treatment outcome correlation tracking
- Best practices linked to case types
- Path: lib/research.ts
Importance Score: 80/100

## Key Relationships

1. Case-Resource Mapping
- Cases link to multiple resource types through service flags
- Bidirectional tracking of resource effectiveness
- Treatment provider scoring based on case requirements
Importance Score: 85/100

2. Knowledge-Case Integration
- Clinical protocols map to case intervention strategies
- Local partnerships connect through service categorization
- Evidence-based practices inform case recommendations
Importance Score: 80/100

3. Treatment Provider Network
- Regional provider clustering
- Service capability matrix
- Referral path tracking
Importance Score: 75/100

## Data Flow Architecture

1. Case Planning Flow
- Client needs assessment → Resource matching → Plan generation
- Integrates knowledge base protocols during plan creation
- Tracks intervention outcomes back to resource effectiveness
Importance Score: 85/100

2. Resource Recommendation Pipeline
- Provider proximity scoring
- Service capability matching
- Outcome-based prioritization
Importance Score: 80/100

